# pipenv
#   According to the pypipenv documentation
#   https://pipenv.readthedocs.io/en/latest/
#   Not all of these are relevant to this project but are included to be safe.
#   See: https://pipenv.readthedocs.io/en/latest/stdlib.html#pipenv
#   and https://pipenv.readthedocs.io/en/latest/stdlib.html#os.environ
Pipfile
Pipfile.lock

# Poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock is generally recommended to be committed
#   in a repo, but this is a exception for an example project.
#   Poetry follows the same logic as Pipfile.lock in that it is primarily a lock
#   file for use by CI and local development, and is not intended to be
#   published. As such, we recommend that it not be committed to version control.
#   If you decide to include it in your version control, you should add the
#   `poetry export` command to your CI pipeline to ensure that the dependencies
#   are installed correctly from the lock file.
poetry.lock

